cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the accompanying paper."
type: software
title: "Affine obstructions and finite-pattern synchronization for the Collatz map"
authors:
  - family-names: Valbuena
    given-names: Lucas
repository-code: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
url: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
abstract: >-
  Lean proofs and a paper showing that nonnegative real affine interpretations
  in two coordinates, with first diagonal entry at least one for every symbol,
  have zero first-coordinate offset gap for every rule whenever all eleven
  rules of the Yolcu–Aaronson–Heule Collatz system are weakly oriented
  coefficientwise. The result holds separately for the original system and
  its word reversal. A second theorem removes the diagonal bounds for the
  reversed system: all eleven weak comparisons force equality of the full
  offset vectors in both eligible TOP rules, da to d and db to dg.
  A separate theorem constructs arbitrarily large translates of every finite
  pattern of nonnegative offsets whose Collatz trajectories first reach one
  at the same finite time, with equal odd counts. Consecutive runs of every
  prescribed length follow. These results do not prove the Collatz conjecture.
keywords:
  - Collatz conjecture
  - string rewriting
  - matrix interpretations
  - Lean
  - formal verification
